=== refused HF-vs-llama adjudications (D-26 clause 3) ===
refused[1] activation-width
    observation: the HF chain records activations as bf16 (dtype field of each record in checkpoints/dump-manifest-chain-2026-10-26.json), llama.cpp records the same stages as f32 (dtype field per row of checkpoints/llama-dump-manifest-2026-10-27-run-a.json). Two numeric systems on the same stage.
    why-refused: D-26 clause 3: llama.cpp is the oracle for engine/*, but a quantized oracle may only ADD checks, never loosen one; calling f32 'the reference' would license a wider input than the bf16 fixture we are gated on, and calling bf16 the reference would loosen llama. Not adjudicated; the user's ±1-ULP policy (D-17) is where this belongs.
refused[2] router renormalisation dtype and form
    observation: llama renormalises the top-k weights with a f32 DIV (graph 1 block 0 node 74 ffn_moe_weights_norm, op DIV, shape [8, 11, 1, 1]); the HF form casts the renormalised weights back to the logits dtype before multiplying the expert output, and our §11.6 fixture already refused the f32 carry at ndiff=1326 with a flipped argmax (engine/HANDOFF.md §MoE renormalisation dtype). The pinned fixture sides with HF; llama disagrees with the fixture.
    why-refused: D-26 clause 3 — recorded as a named divergence, not settled. Settling it would either move our §11.6 must-catch set (a gate change) or declare the oracle wrong; both are the user's.
refused[3] softmax domain before top-k
    observation: llama takes SOFT_MAX over all 256 router logits (graph 1 block 0 node 66, shape [256, 11, 1, 1]) and then selects and renormalises; §03.2 softmaxes the top-k subset after selection. Mathematically the renormalised results agree; bitwise they will not, and the banded/quantized router path can flip a near-tie.
    why-refused: same refusal as above; also unmeasurable today because the stimuli differ.
refused[4] chained-vs-real activations at layers 38 and 39
    observation: the HF chain is not a contiguous run: layer1's input is layer0's output, but layer38's input is layer1's output with layers 2..37 absent (why_not_contiguous / chain_range in checkpoints/dump-manifest-chain-2026-10-26.json). llama's graph-1 layer-38 activation is a real forward over all 40 layers.
    why-refused: Even under an aligned stimulus a layer-38/39 HF-vs-llama delta would mix a chain gap with an implementation difference. The comparable HF-vs-llama scope is layer0 and layer1; layers 38 and 39 are structural-only regardless of stimulus. Reported, not adjudicated.
